 fact that his name is Jeff and he's a  Texas Ranger isn't even revealed until  the series finale is also impossible to  understand because he speaks in a rapid  by a Texas drawl take what man don't  take that and DMV meant I'm a picnic  o'hare hoody that day men on for dangle  years we don't go looking at Cokie  Roberts man Mike judge voiced the  character and as he mentioned on an  episode of Jimmy Kimmel Live he based  his technique on an irate TV viewer who  once left him an incomprehensible  voicemail to complain about judges  previous show a beavis and butthead this  message turned out he goes  I've been calling Alfred a month now  grab batch oh every time it banging up  Kobe's butthole from the tail of Dale  the role of chain-smoking conspiracy  theorists and exterminator Dale Gribble  was almost played by Daniel Stern the  home alone star and the Wonder Years  narrator but he reportedly wanted too  much money and producers sent him away  he would have joined a voice cast I was  populated by well-known actors and  experienced vocal talent prepare to be  destroyed by the deadliest of all  martial arts around the same time king  of the hill co-creator Greg Daniels took  in a Comedy Showcase at the Los Angeles  Club where a Texas born comic named  Johnny Hardwick told some stories about  his family and upbringing  after his sets Daniels offered him a job  as a writer on king of the hill once in  the fold Hardwick auditioned for Dale  telling the Austin Chronicle that he  took inspiration for his  characterization from counterculture  icon William s Burroughs and Matthew  McConaughey in Dazed and Confused along  with a bit of Jack Nicholson Hardwick  got the part of course his first ever  acting gig where is Allen the hill  family lives in Arlen a sleepy  medium-sized city in Texas about a  hundred miles from Dallas or is it like  Springfield or Shelbyville in the  Simpsons  Allen isn't a real place the town's name  is reminiscent of Garland a suburb of  Dallas w